# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-15: the serialization/ round,
commit 2 - the links on the public declarations (decision 4 b), which
the hand-over expected to shrink to quoting.h, the folder's only file
exporting anything.

# Decided
- trueqbit took Claude's leans: quote_identifier ->
  https://www.sqlite.org/lang_keywords.html (no anchor on the page; it
  holds the four quotings, the double quotes making an identifier);
  quote_string_literal, quote_blob_literal ->
  https://www.sqlite.org/lang_expr.html#literal_values_constants_ ("A
  string constant is formed by enclosing the string in single quotes
  ... BLOB literals are string literals containing hexadecimal data and
  preceded by a single "x" or "X" character"); sql_escape no link.
  Links in the form of the builtin round (a line of their own after an
  empty comment line, as dbstat.h).
- quote_blob_literal's doc-comment, old words: "Quote the given string
  value using single quotes, escape containing single quotes by
  doubling them." - false, it escapes nothing; new: "Quote the given
  hexadecimal text as a BLOB literal, `x'...'`; the text is written as
  it is given."

# Discussed
- Found while checking the new comment: its only caller,
  statement_serializer's do_serialize(const std::vector<char>&), passes
  field_printer<std::vector<char>>'s output, which streams each char
  after `ss << std::hex` - std::hex affects integers alone, so the
  bytes come out raw, not as hex digits. Where a blob is serialized as
  a literal rather than bound (dump(), a default value), the SQL holds
  x'<raw bytes>'. Reported to trueqbit; out of a docs commit's scope.
- Green: pre-commit.sh 0; token streams identical; clang-format 20
  unchanged; no "on purpose:".

